# Where an image may have several instances, the test outside fast code whether a value is a closure of one function, whose closures are allocated, is one call of a stub that takes the upper half of the function's closure word and answers in the flags: the Structure of a closure as created, the cell type, the realm and the function number of a closure that has got properties are tested there, once for the program. The one closure of a declared function is still tested by its address
# FORM: AsRead
# OPTIONS: heat=EverythingIsCold disable=pass:InlineCalls disable=flow:ReachedFunctions
# RUN: generate-code calls
# RUN(X64): generate-code
# REQUIRES(X64): x86_64
# RUN(IR): pipeline Select

module m0 path="main.js" displayPath="main.js" body=f0
entry module=m0
variable g0 name="declared" module=m0 declared={type=function} initialization=Function function=f1
function f0 name="main" kind=Module results=[{type=anything}] {
  b0():
    v0 = GetModuleVariable variable=g0
    v1 = NewClosure function=f2
    v2 = NewClosure function=f3
    v3 = NewClosure function=f4
    v4 = Builtin builtin=GlobalThis
    v5 = PropGet v4 key="register" [isFreeName]
    v6 = Call v5, -, v0, v1, v2, v3
    Return v6
}
function f1 name="declared" results=[{type=anything}] {
  b0():
    Return
}
function f2 name="allocated" results=[{type=anything}] {
  b0():
    Return
}
function f3 name="callsDeclared" parameters=[{type=f1 flags=[IsExpected]}] results=[{type=anything}] {
  b0(v0: f1):
    v1 = Call v0
    Return v1
}
function f4 name="callsAllocated" parameters=[{type=f2 flags=[IsExpected]}] results=[{type=anything}] {
  b0(v0: f2):
    v1 = Call v0
    Return v1
}
# IR-LABEL: function f3 name="callsDeclared"
# IR: = IsClosureOf v0 function=f1
# IR-LABEL: function f4 name="callsAllocated"
# IR: = IsClosureOf v0 function=f2
# CHECK: f3: size=
# CHECK-NOT: stub ValueIsClosureOf
# CHECK: f4: size=
# CHECK: stub ValueIsClosureOf x1
# X64: f4: size=41 frame
